[38;2;124;124;124m$IB = B$ means $1 \in IB$. We have $A/I \to B/IB$. Since $B$ is faithfully flat [0m[38;2;124;124;124mover $A$, $A/I = 0$ iff $B/IB = 0$ (because $B/IB = B \otimes_A A/I$, and [0m
[38;2;124;124;124mfaithful flatness means $M = 0$ iff $B \otimes_A M = 0$). So $B/IB = 0$ iff $A/I[0m[38;2;124;124;124m= 0$ iff $I = A$.[0m

[38;2;124;124;124mSo: $I \cdot \mathbb{C}[x_1, \ldots, x_n] = \mathbb{C}[x_1, \ldots, x_n]$ [0m
